clk: rockchip: rk3288: let i2s0_clkout set its parent's rate

i2s0_clkout is the I2S MCLK output pin, usually the codec's master clock.
Codec drivers such as rt5640 call clk_set_rate() on it with 256 * fs.
Without CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT the mux can only pick a parent whose rate is
already at most the request, so switching from 48 kHz to 44.1 kHz fails
with -EINVAL (both i2s_pre at 12.288 MHz and xin12m are above
11.2896 MHz). Let it adjust i2s_pre, the fractional I2S clock that the
I2S controller sets to the same rate anyway, like clk_i2sout on rk3399.

--- a/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3288.c	2026-10-21 15:45:51
+++ b/drivers/clk/rockchip/clk-rk3288.c	2026-10-21 15:45:51
@@ -364,7 +364,7 @@
 			RK3288_CLKSEL_CON(8), 0,
 			RK3288_CLKGATE_CON(4), 2, GFLAGS,
 			&rk3288_i2s_fracmux),
-	COMPOSITE_NODIV(SCLK_I2S0_OUT, "i2s0_clkout", mux_i2s_clkout_p, 0,
+	COMPOSITE_NODIV(SCLK_I2S0_OUT, "i2s0_clkout", mux_i2s_clkout_p, CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
 			RK3288_CLKSEL_CON(4), 12, 1, MFLAGS,
 			RK3288_CLKGATE_CON(4), 0, GFLAGS),
 	GATE(SCLK_I2S0, "sclk_i2s0", "i2s_pre", CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT,
